    thinking: "**Defining Puzzle Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting to sketch out the specifics for the daily puzzle feature. I\'m focusing on the technical requirements now, like how to reliably fetch a new puzzle every day and integrate it seamlessly into the main menu as a distinct game mode.\n\n\n**Outlining New Mode**\n\nI\'ve been mapping out the \'daily_puzzle\' mode more concretely. It\342\200\231s now clear it needs a dynamic timer, daily updates, and an archive to allow access to past puzzles. I\'m imagining a rich UI with difficulty ratings, hints, and a share button. Success should award respect, Elo, and a streak counter.\n\n\n**Integrating Daily Puzzle Mode**\n\nI\'m making progress by integrating the new daily puzzle mode. I\'ve updated the `GameMode` type to include \'daily_puzzle\'. I\'ve also identified a good data source for a tactical puzzles archive. Now I\'m focused on developing the features for dynamic fetching and puzzle generation.\n\n\n**Implementing Daily Puzzle Logic**\n\nI\'ve been working on `src/utils/dailyPuzzles.ts`. It\'s starting to take shape: a date-based hash for puzzle generation, API fallback, and a countdown timer. I\'m focusing on local storage and Firestore integration for solve history. Also, I\'m developing the calendar browser for past puzzles.\n\nLet\'s check every component to ensure that the new `GameMode` is added, including adding the \"Daily Puzzle\" features in the header and in the game selection modal. I\'m enhancing either the `PuzzleMode.tsx` or developing a dedicated `DailyPuzzleView.tsx` with a 24-hour countdown.\n\n\n"
