    thinking: "**Designing the Challenge**\n\nI\'m deep in the design phase, mapping out a dynamic daily tactical challenge. My focus is on creating a fresh, engaging experience that refreshes every 24 hours. The goal is a seamless addition to the current game mode.\n\n\n**Implementing the Mechanics**\n\nOkay, I\'m making headway on the technical implementation. The `GameMode` type in `chess.ts` has been updated to include \'daily_puzzle\'. I\'ve also begun adding fields to `DailyPuzzleData` to handle extra puzzle details. Now I\'m focused on the daily puzzles system. I\'m building the deterministic algorithm that will fetch the puzzle based on the date, along with the real-time countdown timer.\n\n\n**Adding Historical Review**\n\nI\'ve been thinking about enhancing the daily challenge with historical review. I\'m implementing an archive and calendar feature, allowing players to revisit past daily puzzles and track their progress. I\'m also planning an online fallback mechanism for fetching puzzles, using Lichess\' API, ensuring the game mode functions well even offline. I\'m going to synchronize progress with Cloud Firestore to make sure the user\'s solved status and streaks can persist across devices. The final piece is the dedicated game mode view, including a countdown and branding.\n\n\n**Refining the UI**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in the user interface specifics. I\'m focusing on the archive/calendar modal, giving it solve status badges and the ability to switch dates. The interactive chessboard is also coming together, with visual move indicators, turn indicators, and move progression steps. I\'ve designed tactical assistant tools like Scout Hint, Show Solution, Reset, and an online refresh option. Finally, I\'m working on the tactical lore box, including theme badges, difficulty ratings, and grandmaster backstories to enhance the player\'s experience.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 614951772
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
