  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Authoring Utilities**\n\nI\'m currently focused on building the `authoringService.ts`. I\'m going to start with a local storage-based persistence strategy, which will then synchronize with Firestore if it\'s available. I\'m aiming to implement the key methods first: Save, Update, Delete, and Publish for authored puzzles. I\'ll also be including a method for loading the user\'s authored puzzles.\n\n\n**Expanding Community Features**\n\nI\'m now thinking about community-authored puzzles. I\'ll need to allow users to like, rate, and solve these community creations. I\'m also looking at incorporating a logging service to track match logs and system audit entries. This will involve saving match records for various game modes, filtering and exporting logs, and also importing PGN files. I want to build out the authoring view and logging view components, incorporating features like a board position editor, move recorder, and metadata forms within the authoring view. The logging view will contain match logs, system activity, stat summaries, and interactive detail, and a match log list. I\'m imagining a component to import and export PGN files.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 900555067
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
