  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Profile Picture Changes**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how users change their profile pictures within `ProfileModal.tsx`. I\'m starting by understanding the different pathways a user can take: clicking the avatar itself, clicking \"AI Avatar Studio\", or selecting the \"Edit\" option. My next step will be to map out the specific actions triggered by each of these selections.\n\n\n**Refining Avatar Editing Flow**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Edit\" mode within the profile picture functionality. I\'m prioritizing user experience with a \"Change Profile Picture\" section that supports direct uploads (instant conversion to base64, saves to Firestore and local storage), image URL input with live preview, preset avatar selections (Peshmerga/Kurdish themes), and a direct link to the AI Avatar Generator Studio. Crucially, any new avatar selection or generation triggers immediate and permanent saves to Firestore, Firebase Auth, local state, and localStorage for robust persistence.\n\n\n"
