  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Potential Errors**\n\nI\'m currently considering scenarios where `updateDoc` might fail, specifically if the user document doesn\'t exist or if permissions are an issue. To mitigate these situations, I\'m leaning towards using `setDoc` with the `merge: true` option. This approach should reliably update the document, even if it\'s being created for the first time.\n\n\n**Refining Avatar Logic**\n\nI\'ve significantly refined the avatar handling. I\'m now implementing logic to manage profile photo updates across multiple scenarios: when a `details.photoURL` is provided, I\'m integrating `firebaseUpdateProfile`, local storage caching, and handling of specific account types (Sky, Developer). Furthermore, I\'ve developed the loading profiles logic to prioritize cached avatars from local storage, gracefully merging them with existing data or defaulting to system avatars, which should improve performance.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 445809823
    }
