  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating the Design**\n\nI\'ve started sketching out the Login Page and User Profile Page, keeping in mind the user\'s need for a chess web app. I\'m focusing on UI/UX principles to create a user-friendly and aesthetically pleasing experience. The full-stack development considerations are next on my agenda.\n\n\n**Defining the Pages**\n\nI\'ve specified the components needed for the login and user profile pages. For the login, there\'s a logo and slogan, multiple authentication options including social logins, and a guest access option, all within a dark-mode theme. The user profile will include avatar and stats, along with Elo ratings for various time controls, a rating progress chart, and a recent match history list. The design elements will improve user accessibility.\n\n\n**Adding Player Stats**\n\nI\'m now integrating player statistics and achievement badges into the User Profile. Specifically, I am focusing on breakdowns of wins, losses, and draws by piece color, and incorporating an achievement badge section to celebrate milestones. I plan to provide the user with clear visualizations of game accuracy and rating changes.\n\n\n**Refining Authentication Methods**\n\nI am currently focusing on refining the login page\'s authentication methods. I\'m adding Google and Apple OAuth buttons with sleek SVG icons, aiming for a smooth integration with Firebase and user-friendly notifications. I\'m also adding a standard email/password form with login/register toggles, show/hide password, \"Remember Me,\" and \"Forgot Password\" functionality. A guest access option is in the plan, along with a dev/master quick access switcher, all with clean layouts. I\'m implementing responsive designs with smooth motion transitions, error and success badges.\n\n\n\n**Detailing the Profile**\n\nI\'m now detailing the user profile page\'s elements. I\'ve focused on an \"Online\" toggle/status, and adding action buttons like \"Challenge to Game\" and \"Add Friend.\" There\'s also an Edit Profile button and avatar upload trigger. The ratings card is now organized, with time control data, and peak stats, games played. I\'m also implementing an interactive Elo rating progress chart.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 874855560
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
