  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Initial Requirements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the prompt, specifically breaking down the requirements for both the Login and User Profile pages. It seems like a design and implementation task.\n\n\n**Analyzing Login and Profile**\n\nI\'ve just finished dissecting the login page, focusing on authentication, the guest access option, and the aesthetic elements like the chess-themed slogan. Now, I\'m moving on to the user profile page. I am looking at the profile header, ratings display, rating progress chart, and recent match history components. I\'m noting the data points needed for each section, for later integration.\n\n\n**Defining Component Architecture**\n\nI\'m now outlining the component architecture and state management for both the Login and User Profile pages. I\'m focusing on responsiveness and modern code practices. Dark mode is also being integrated, using a dark palette. I also am looking at how to allow both the Login and Profile views, in various presentation modes. I am preparing to implement `LoginPage.tsx` and `UserProfilePage.tsx`.\n\n\n**Crafting Login Design**\n\nI\'m now deep in the design for `LoginPage.tsx`. The dark slate aesthetic with chessboard background is taking shape nicely. I\'ve got the header with the logo and slogan outlined, and now I\'m working on the social OAuth logins with Google and Apple integrations, complete with their respective icons. I\'m also planning the standard form, including tab switcher, input fields, the \"Remember Me\" checkbox, and the \"Forgot Password\" action.\n\n\n**Refining Login Features**\n\nI\'m now refining the login experience. I\'ve integrated email input with real `sendPasswordResetEmail` and feedback. I\'m also adding a submit button with a loading spinner, plus error banners. I\'ve implemented a high-contrast guest access button, and quick-switcher buttons to bypass the login for developer and grandmaster test accounts. I am designing a close / back button now.\n\nI\'m now designing `src/components/UserProfilePage.tsx`. I am creating the header, including the user avatar with upload/preset options, username/display name, country flag, and online status selector. I\'m implementing \"Challenge to Game\" and \"Add Friend\" buttons with interactive states.\n\n\n**Constructing Ratings & Charts**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Ratings Card, a 5-card grid for different time controls, each displaying current and peak ratings, total games, and a relevant icon. Then, the Interactive Rating Progress Chart is being crafted, including time range and time control filters. The SVG chart will use high-contrast gradients and interactive elements.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 454130336
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
