  planner_response {
    response: "I have refactored the chess profile and dashboard panel to deliver a clean layout following modern UX design principles:\n\n### Refactored Profile Architecture\n\n- **Clear Tabbed Interface**:\n  - **Overview**: Displays prominent Elo ratings across Rapid, Blitz, Bullet, Daily, and Puzzles, alongside a 30-day sparkline trajectory, piece win rate breakdown, recent matches snapshot, and top honors.\n  - **Match History**: Comprehensive battle log featuring live result badges (Win / Loss / Draw), opponent metadata, Elo delta shifts ($\\pm\\Delta$), move accuracy scores, and a 1-click **Analyze** button linking directly into the engine analysis board. Includes filter pills and real-time search.\n  - **Analytics**: Full-scale interactive SVG Rating Trajectory with timeframe filters (`1W`, `1M`, `1Y`, `ALL`), interactive data point inspection, opening repertoire win-rate meters, and tactical precision telemetry.\n  - **Social**: Friends list with online status indicators, quick broadcast status switcher (\360\237\237\242 *Online*, \342\232\224\357\270\217 *In-Game*, \342\232\252 *Offline*), and an 8-badge achievement showcase.\n\n- **Visual Hierarchy & Typography**:\n  - Primary Elo numbers are styled in bold, high-contrast monospace display typography (`text-3xl font-black font-mono text-white`).\n  - Secondary attributes (time control, game counts, opening names, dates) are styled in muted Slate tones (`text-xs text-slate-400 font-medium`) to eliminate visual noise.\n\n- **Modular Rounded Cards & Subtle Borders**:\n  - Grouped related components into `rounded-2xl` and `rounded-3xl` Slate/Zinc cards (`bg-slate-900/90 border border-slate-800`) with soft depth and ample inner padding.\n\n- **Responsive 2-Column Desktop Grid**:\n  - Desktop view utilizes a structured multi-column split (primary metrics and analytics on the left, side snapshots and social controls on the right), which smoothly collapses into a single column on mobile screens."
    modified_response: "I have refactored the chess profile and dashboard panel to deliver a clean layout following modern UX design principles:\n\n### Refactored Profile Architecture\n\n- **Clear Tabbed Interface**:\n  - **Overview**: Displays prominent Elo ratings across Rapid, Blitz, Bullet, Daily, and Puzzles, alongside a 30-day sparkline trajectory, piece win rate breakdown, recent matches snapshot, and top honors.\n  - **Match History**: Comprehensive battle log featuring live result badges (Win / Loss / Draw), opponent metadata, Elo delta shifts ($\\pm\\Delta$), move accuracy scores, and a 1-click **Analyze** button linking directly into the engine analysis board. Includes filter pills and real-time search.\n  - **Analytics**: Full-scale interactive SVG Rating Trajectory with timeframe filters (`1W`, `1M`, `1Y`, `ALL`), interactive data point inspection, opening repertoire win-rate meters, and tactical precision telemetry.\n  - **Social**: Friends list with online status indicators, quick broadcast status switcher (\360\237\237\242 *Online*, \342\232\224\357\270\217 *In-Game*, \342\232\252 *Offline*), and an 8-badge achievement showcase.\n\n- **Visual Hierarchy & Typography**:\n  - Primary Elo numbers are styled in bold, high-contrast monospace display typography (`text-3xl font-black font-mono text-white`).\n  - Secondary attributes (time control, game counts, opening names, dates) are styled in muted Slate tones (`text-xs text-slate-400 font-medium`) to eliminate visual noise.\n\n- **Modular Rounded Cards & Subtle Borders**:\n  - Grouped related components into `rounded-2xl` and `rounded-3xl` Slate/Zinc cards (`bg-slate-900/90 border border-slate-800`) with soft depth and ample inner padding.\n\n- **Responsive 2-Column Desktop Grid**:\n  - Desktop view utilizes a structured multi-column split (primary metrics and analytics on the left, side snapshots and social controls on the right), which smoothly collapses into a single column on mobile screens."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
