    thinking: "**Analyzing Layout Considerations**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently assessing the layout behavior of the `App.tsx` component, specifically focusing on how `justify-center` impacts centering content within the `main` element when the `activeMode` is not a board page. I\'ve noted that using `justify-center` along with `flex-1 flex flex-col justify-center` can introduce scrolling problems on smaller screens. I\'m considering using `justify-start` or implementing conditional logic to achieve the desired layout without the scrolling issues.\n\n\n**Refining Scroll Mechanics**\n\nI\'ve been looking at how to make sure we have smooth top-to-bottom scrolling in profile page mode. I\'m thinking that setting `activeMode === \'profile_page\'` or giving it `min-h-0` will do the trick. Also, changing the root `min-h-screen` to `min-h-[100dvh] flex flex-col` seems like a good solution for layout. Now, I\'m getting into the nitty-gritty of the specific header redesign for different screen sizes, so I am going to explore the mobile version first.\n\n\n**Designing Mobile Interface**\n\nOkay, I\'m focusing on the mobile version now. I want to make sure the body can scroll smoothly with `overflow-y: auto`. I am looking at how to make horizontal, swipeable tabs and a fixed bottom navigation bar for panel switching. I\'ll test out a top scrollable pill bar, or a bottom navigation bar. Touch target size is another key area, so I am going to make sure everything meets the minimum 44x44px.\n\n\n"
