  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Mobile Header Design**\n\nI\'m now diving into the mobile design for the UserProfilePage. The current focus is on a header redesign. For screens smaller than 768px, the requirement is to condense the header into a 56px sticky bar. This bar will display only the avatar, display name, and country flag.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Panel Design**\n\nI\'m now focusing on mobile panel visibility and responsiveness, ensuring smooth scrolling with `overflow-y: auto`. I\'m exploring horizontal swipeable tabs or a fixed bottom navigation for easy panel switching. I\'m also ensuring the viewport height is correctly handled using `100dvh` to prevent clipping. UI scaling is also a focus, increasing touch targets to 44x44px and adjusting the minimum font size to 14px. I\'m adding padding to prevent content from touching screen edges.\n\n\n**Designing Mobile UI Structure**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI structure. The main container will use `min-h-[100dvh] flex flex-col` in `App.tsx` and the UserProfilePage component will utilize flexbox for layout, using `flex-1 flex flex-col ... min-h-0`. I\'m using `justify-start overflow-y-auto` for the profile page mode. Also, I\'m integrating a sticky 56px header for mobile screens that shows an avatar, name, flag, and a primary rating badge. The right side will feature an interactive quick action button.\n\n\n**Implementing Mobile Drawer**\n\nI\'m now implementing the mobile drawer/bottom sheet design. It will be triggered by a toggle button or header tap. Inside, I\'m incorporating a drag handle, full avatar, status selector, action buttons, and a multi-rating quick view. I\'m also including a close button. The drawer\'s height will be constrained to `85dvh`.\n\n\n**Examining Detailed UI Elements**\n\nNow, I\'m analyzing the detailed view, which is rendered with a blur effect and shadow. It features the Kurdish accent bar, avatar with edit hover, username, honor badges, quote, full action buttons (Challenge, Add Friend, etc.), and respect points. I\'m also examining the tab and navigation structure, specifically the mobile and desktop variations. On mobile, there are horizontal swipeable tabs and a fixed bottom navigation bar with icons, labels, and badge counts. Desktop uses sleek top tabs. I\'m checking touch targets and typography details.\n\n\n**Detailing Mobile Tab Views**\n\nI\'m now detailing the individual elements across various panels. The Overview tab will include distinct cards for ratings, sparkline progress, piece performance, recent matches, and top honors, each adhering to specific styling for readability and touch targets. I am also working on the Match History/Games tab, which will include filter pills, a search input, and match item cards, all optimized for mobile use.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 375953280
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
