    thinking: "**Adjusting Layout Logic**\n\nI\'ve been working on refining the layout in `App.tsx`. I\'ve updated the `<main>` element\'s `className` attribute. It now incorporates a conditional logic based on the `activeMode` state. This makes dynamic adjustments to the flexbox properties, and also enables `overflow-y-auto` when the profile page is active.\n\n\n**Revising Profile Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `UserProfilePage.tsx` component. The focus is on a mobile-first approach for the header. I\'m crafting a sticky top bar with a sleek design. I\'ve designed the mobile (<768px) structure with an avatar, display name, country flag, Elo badge, and quick challenge button all in the works for a user-friendly layout.\n\n\n**Designing Mobile Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing the expandable mobile profile drawer. It\'ll be a fixed, full-screen overlay with a backdrop. I\'m focusing on user-friendly elements: a drag handle, a full profile card with interactive elements (avatar picker!), status selection buttons with large touch targets, and action buttons for key functions like challenging or adding friends. The grid cards for rating summaries and a clear close button with 44px touch targets are also in progress.\n\n\n**Optimizing Mobile Layout**\n\nI\'m focusing on ensuring content isn\'t clipped on mobile. I\'ve set the container to `min-h-[100dvh]` with `h-full overflow-y-auto` and `pb-20`. I\'m implementing horizontal swipeable tabs across both desktop and mobile using the `md:flex overflow-x-auto no-scrollbar scroll-smooth gap-2 pb-2` class. Plus, I\'m designing a fixed bottom navigation bar on mobile with clear icons and labels, including \'Overview,\' \'Games,\' \'Stats,\' and \'Social.\'\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI Scaling & Touch Targets. All buttons, tabs, pills, and filter toggles now have `min-h-[44px]` (or `min-w-[44px]` for square action icons) and generous hit areas. All body texts, card titles, opponent names, and descriptions now use minimum 14px (`text-sm`) base font size for crystal.\n\n\n"
