  planner_response {
    response: "I have refactored the profile and dashboard UI with mobile-first optimizations:\n\n### 1. Responsive Header Architecture\n- **Mobile Viewport (< 768px)**:\n  - Collapsed the header into a **56px sticky bar** (`h-14`) displaying only the user\'s **Avatar**, **Display Name**, **Country Flag**, and **Primary Elo rating badge** (`2240 Rapid`).\n  - Added an expandable **Profile Drawer** (bottom sheet) that opens on tap, housing broadcast status toggles (\360\237\237\242 *Online*, \342\232\224\357\270\217 *In-Game*, \342\232\252 *Offline*), full honor titles, custom status quotes, respect scores, and primary action buttons (*Challenge*, *Add Friend*, *Share Profile*, *Edit Settings*, *Avatar Editor*).\n- **Desktop Viewport ($\\ge$ 768px)**:\n  - Preserved the full header hero card with the Kurdish tricolor accent bar, quick action buttons, hover avatar customization, and respect points pill.\n\n### 2. Panel Visibility & Navigation\n- **Dynamic Viewport Height**: Updated root and container heights to `min-h-[100dvh]` to prevent address bar clipping on iOS Safari and Android Chrome.\n- **Scrollable Panels**: Main body container uses `overflow-y: auto` with `min-h-0` and safe bottom padding (`pb-24`), preventing panels from being cut off.\n- **Mobile Navigation**: Implemented top horizontal swipeable tabs along with a fixed **Mobile Bottom Navigation Bar** for fast 1-tap switching across **Overview**, **Games**, **Stats**, and **Social**.\n\n### 3. UI Scaling & Touch Targets\n- **44x44px Touch Targets**: Configured all interactive controls, filter pills (`ALL`, `WIN`, `LOSS`, `DRAW`, `1W`, `1M`, `1Y`), search inputs, tabs, and action buttons to a minimum size of 44x44px.\n- **Enhanced Typography**: Set base panel text, opponent names, ratings, and descriptions to at least 14px (`text-sm`) for readability on mobile displays.\n- **Spacing & Padding**: Added consistent outer gutters and inner card padding (`px-4 py-3` / `p-4 sm:p-5`) to eliminate edge-clipping."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Design Completion**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the linting and compilation steps completed without issue. Now, I\'m shifting my focus to reviewing the optimizations implemented, specifically the header redesign, against the stated user requirements. The mobile view (< 768px) is collapsed into a 56px sticky bar, displaying only the Avatar and Display.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have refactored the profile and dashboard UI with mobile-first optimizations:\n\n### 1. Responsive Header Architecture\n- **Mobile Viewport (< 768px)**:\n  - Collapsed the header into a **56px sticky bar** (`h-14`) displaying only the user\'s **Avatar**, **Display Name**, **Country Flag**, and **Primary Elo rating badge** (`2240 Rapid`).\n  - Added an expandable **Profile Drawer** (bottom sheet) that opens on tap, housing broadcast status toggles (\360\237\237\242 *Online*, \342\232\224\357\270\217 *In-Game*, \342\232\252 *Offline*), full honor titles, custom status quotes, respect scores, and primary action buttons (*Challenge*, *Add Friend*, *Share Profile*, *Edit Settings*, *Avatar Editor*).\n- **Desktop Viewport ($\\ge$ 768px)**:\n  - Preserved the full header hero card with the Kurdish tricolor accent bar, quick action buttons, hover avatar customization, and respect points pill.\n\n### 2. Panel Visibility & Navigation\n- **Dynamic Viewport Height**: Updated root and container heights to `min-h-[100dvh]` to prevent address bar clipping on iOS Safari and Android Chrome.\n- **Scrollable Panels**: Main body container uses `overflow-y: auto` with `min-h-0` and safe bottom padding (`pb-24`), preventing panels from being cut off.\n- **Mobile Navigation**: Implemented top horizontal swipeable tabs along with a fixed **Mobile Bottom Navigation Bar** for fast 1-tap switching across **Overview**, **Games**, **Stats**, and **Social**.\n\n### 3. UI Scaling & Touch Targets\n- **44x44px Touch Targets**: Configured all interactive controls, filter pills (`ALL`, `WIN`, `LOSS`, `DRAW`, `1W`, `1M`, `1Y`), search inputs, tabs, and action buttons to a minimum size of 44x44px.\n- **Enhanced Typography**: Set base panel text, opponent names, ratings, and descriptions to at least 14px (`text-sm`) for readability on mobile displays.\n- **Spacing & Padding**: Added consistent outer gutters and inner card padding (`px-4 py-3` / `p-4 sm:p-5`) to eliminate edge-clipping."
