  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Interaction Methods**\n\nI\'m now investigating the potential causes of unresponsive piece movement, specifically focusing on the `ChessBoard.tsx` file. I\'m carefully scrutinizing the click and drag interactions. I\'m paying close attention to the `onClick` handler applied to each square, as it might be a source of the issue.\n\n\n**Analyzing Click Sequence**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on the click sequence logic in `ChessBoard.tsx`. Specifically, I am trying to determine what is going on with the interactions. It is clear that `onMouseDown` fires first, followed by `onMouseUp`, which in turn leads to the firing of `onClick` if the mouse is released on the same square. This means `selectedSquare` can be set and immediately unset due to the `onClick` handler. This could cause some issues! I\'m now exploring how the `selectedSquare` and `draggingSquare` states interplay during these events.\n\n\n**Uncovering Single-Click Bug**\n\nI\'ve made a crucial discovery: single clicks immediately deselect pieces!  The `onClick` handler is immediately deselecting pieces selected by `onMouseDown` or `onTouchStart`. I\'m starting to grasp how this is causing the glitchy behavior.  On both desktop and mobile, a single click or tap, after an initial selection, unintentionally deselects the piece! This is definitely what is going on with the click-to-move issue.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 299671519
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
