  planner_response {
    response: "I have fixed and upgraded the chess piece movement system:\n\n- **Click-to-Move Reliability**: Resolved the event race condition where mouse/touch releases on a square were prematurely deselecting the active piece. Clicking or tapping a piece now reliably selects it, renders the legal move indicators and capture rings, and allows single-tap destination moves.\n- **Drag-and-Drop Precision**: Added a distance threshold ($4\\text{px}$) to cleanly separate clicks from drags. Dragging pieces now utilizes GPU-accelerated hardware transforms (`translate3d`), with accurate board-boundary clamping and coordinate resolution for both standard and flipped board orientations.\n- **Mobile Touch Handling**: Configured touch listeners with `touch-action: none` to eliminate viewport drag interference and gestures, allowing smooth drag-and-drop and tap-to-move interactions on touchscreens.\n- **Move Validation & Synchronous Execution**: Moved legal-move calculation to synchronous evaluation, preventing drop-action misses caused by asynchronous state batching."
    modified_response: "I have fixed and upgraded the chess piece movement system:\n\n- **Click-to-Move Reliability**: Resolved the event race condition where mouse/touch releases on a square were prematurely deselecting the active piece. Clicking or tapping a piece now reliably selects it, renders the legal move indicators and capture rings, and allows single-tap destination moves.\n- **Drag-and-Drop Precision**: Added a distance threshold ($4\\text{px}$) to cleanly separate clicks from drags. Dragging pieces now utilizes GPU-accelerated hardware transforms (`translate3d`), with accurate board-boundary clamping and coordinate resolution for both standard and flipped board orientations.\n- **Mobile Touch Handling**: Configured touch listeners with `touch-action: none` to eliminate viewport drag interference and gestures, allowing smooth drag-and-drop and tap-to-move interactions on touchscreens.\n- **Move Validation & Synchronous Execution**: Moved legal-move calculation to synchronous evaluation, preventing drop-action misses caused by asynchronous state batching."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
