  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing AOT Theme Engine**\n\nI\'m starting to break down the Attack on Titan theme engine requirements. First up: the board theme. I\'ve noted a few potential IDs: `aot`, `attack_on_titan`, or `wall_maria`. I\'m leaning towards `aot` for brevity, but I\'ll consider the others later.\n\n\n**Defining Theme Parameters**\n\nI\'ve got the `aot` theme IDs added to the `BoardThemeId` and `PieceThemeId` types within the chess code. I\'m focusing on the board aesthetics now. I\'m aiming for a dark fantasy feel inspired by Wall Maria, with weathered stone textures for the dark squares, and a Survey Corps green tint for the light squares. I\'m also planning to use an SVG overlay or CSS pattern for the stone texture. Active moves will get a green ODM gas glow, while checks will have a red steam animation, both effects I\'ve defined.\n\n\n**Incorporating New Visuals**\n\nI\'m now integrating the visual concepts I have planned. I\'m imagining rivets and dark slate outlines for the board. Also, I\'m leaning toward a subtle Wall Maria watermark, perhaps the emblem or the Wings of Freedom. For piece theming, the Survey Corps are white, with King Erwin, Queen Mikasa, Bishop Levi/Hange, and Knight ODM gear motifs.\n\n\n**Visualizing Character Designs**\n\nI\'m developing the Attack on Titan chess piece designs now. For white, I\'m imagining the Survey Corps and their equipment: Erwin, Mikasa, Levi, Hange, and ODM gear. For the black pieces, I\'m leaning towards the Titans and Marley forces. The King will be the Colossal Titan, the Queen the Female Titan, Bishops Beast and Jaw Titan, Knights the Cart and Sprinting Titan, Rooks the Armored Titan, and Pawns the Pure Titan. I\'ll need to figure out how to best represent these elements visually.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 774319806
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
