  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Crafting ODM Animations**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the custom CSS animations for the Attack on Titan theme, specifically the ODM gear\'s emerald gas glow aura. I\'ve started the `@keyframes` rule for `aot-odm-gas-pulse`, working on the `box-shadow` property and its pulse effect. I\'m aiming for a distinct visual representation of the gas jets.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Effects**\n\nI\'ve been iterating on the Attack on Titan ODM gear\'s emerald gas glow. I\'ve adjusted the box-shadow properties within the `@keyframes` to create a more dynamic pulse. I\'ve also integrated an additional animation for the drifting vapor effect. I\'m satisfied with the current iterations, however, I plan to compare different timing functions to compare different effects.\n\n\n**Developing Pulse Effects**\n\nNow, I\'m working on a \"steam danger\" animation using a different pulse. I\'ve defined `@keyframes aot-check-steam-pulse` and am working on `background-color` and `box-shadow` properties, for a red-toned, warning effect. I\'m focusing on creating an intense, eye-catching visual cue.\n\n\n**Designing Backgrounds and Pieces**\n\nI\'ve been working on a subtle pattern for the Wall Maria stone background, incorporating radial and linear gradients for a textured look, playing with transparency for depth. The background is almost there! I also plan to add a dedicated component or SVG elements for the Wall Maria watermark, contingent on the `boardTheme` variable. Furthermore, I\'ve got my sights on crafting SVG vector designs for the chess pieces. I\'m keen on bringing the Attack on Titan theme to life.\n\n\n**Conceptualizing Chess Pieces**\n\nI\'m now diving into the chess piece designs, specifically for the White side, the Scout Regiment. I\'ve sketched ideas for each piece: Erwin/Eren for the King, incorporating the crown and ODM blades. Mikasa\'s scarf and swords for the Queen. Levi and Hange\'s emblems are forming the Bishops, Scout horses/ODM gear for the Knights, and Wall Maria towers for the Rooks.\n\n\n**Defining Chess Pieces**\n\nI\'m now detailing the chess piece designs for the Black side (Titans/Marley). I\'ve envisioned the Colossal Titan\'s head as the King, complete with a steam aura and burning eyes. The Queen is the Female Titan in crystal, and for the Bishops, I\'m thinking of the Beast Titan\'s and Jaw Titan\'s jawbones. I\'m imagining the Knights as a sprinting Cart Titan.\n\n\n**Visualizing Titan Piece Designs**\n\nI\'m imagining the Armored Titan\'s hardened plates for the Rooks, complete with crimson glowing vents. For the Pawns, I\'m thinking of a menacing Pure Titan silhouette with glowing eyes. Additionally, I\'m assessing how to best display the Scout Regiment and Marleyan/Titan badges on the player profile cards, considering the emerald and crimson color accents within the `ChessClock.tsx` component to adapt or theme dynamically.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Logic**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the Attack on Titan theme choice throughout the application. I\'m focusing on conditional rendering for the Scout Regiment and Marleyan/Titan badges. I\'ve located `BoardThemeId` and `PieceThemeId` in `src/types/chess.ts`, and I\'m updating `src/utils/themePresets.ts` to include the AoT theme preset with corresponding colors. I\'m verifying the proper application of these color profiles across different UI elements.\n\n\n**Integrating Theme Options**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the Attack on Titan theme into the settings modal. I\'m adding \'aot\' to both `BOARD_THEMES` and `PIECE_THEMES` in `SettingsModal.tsx` and adding theme-specific properties. I\'m also planning to dynamically set `boardTheme` and `pieceTheme` when the `aot` option is selected, mirroring existing behavior of other themes. I\'m aiming for seamless integration.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now implementing theme-specific visual enhancements. For the Attack on Titan theme, active piece moves will showcase an ODM gas glow with drifting particles, while last move highlights will use an emerald exhaust glow. A red steam animation will denote a king in check. Additionally, a Wall Maria watermark with crossed ODM blades is planned for the board background. I\'m also working on Scout Regiment badges and emerald green borders for the bottom player cards when the AoT theme is active.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 51329986
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
