  planner_response {
    response: "I will now build the modular Theme Switcher System with complete SVG piece sets for Batman Gotham City (Heroes vs Villains) and Attack on Titan (Scout Regiment vs Titans), along with Wall Maria, Gotham City, and Classic board styles, and full White/Black faction crossover compatibility.\n\nLet\'s first view `src/types/chess.ts` and `src/components/ChessPiece.tsx`.The following action was requested:\nView contents of file /src/types/chess.ts from lines 1 to 50The action produced the following result:\nFile Path: `/src/types/chess.ts`\nTotal Lines: 269\nTotal Bytes: 6273\nShowing lines 1 to 50\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: export type PieceType = \'p\' | \'n\' | \'b\' | \'r\' | \'q\' | \'k\';\n2: export type PieceColor = \'w\' | \'b\';\n3: \n4: export type BoardThemeId = \'peshmerga\' | \'ukh\' | \'aot\' | \'emerald\' | \'wood\' | \'ocean\' | \'midnight\' | \'marble\' | \'custom\';\n5: export type PieceThemeId = \'peshmerga\' | \'ukh\' | \'aot\' | \'crystal_neon\' | \'fide_3d\' | \'classic\' | \'neo\' | \'alpha\' | \'vintage\';\n6: \n7: export type GameMode = \'ai\' | \'pass_and_play\' | \'daily_puzzle\' | \'puzzle\' | \'analysis\' | \'online_match\' | \'multiplayer\' | \'authoring\' | \'logging\' | \'database\' | \'login\' | \'profile_page\';\n8: \n9: export interface UserSettings {\n10:   boardTheme: BoardThemeId;\n11:   pieceTheme: PieceThemeId;\n12:   soundEnabled: boolean;\n13:   showLegalMoves: boolean;\n14:   showCoordinates: boolean;\n15:   autoPromoteQueen: boolean;\n16:   moveAnimationSpeed: \'fast\' | \'normal\' | \'slow\';\n17:   hapticFeedback: boolean;\n18:   highlightCheck: boolean;\n19:   uiThemeId?: string;\n20: }\n21: \n22: export interface RespectProfile {\n23:   level: number;\n24:   elo: number;\n25:   respectPoints: number;\n26:   honorTier: \'Bronze\' | \'Silver\' | \'Gold\' | \'Platinum\' | \'Diamond\' | \'Grandmaster\' | \'Peshmerga Hero\' | \'UKH Chancellor\' | \'Immortal\';\n27:   streak: number;\n28:   totalWins: number;\n29:   totalGames: number;\n30:   currentTitle: string;\n31:   unlockedTitles: string[];\n32:   unlockedThemes: string[];\n33:   respectHistory: RespectLogEntry[];\n34:   feedbackGivenCount: number;\n35:   isBanned?: boolean;\n36:   isMuted?: boolean;\n37:   avatarUrl?: string;\n38: }\n39: \n40: export interface RespectLogEntry {\n41:   id: string;\n42:   timestamp: number;\n43:   amount: number;\n44:   reason: string;\n45:   actionType: \'win\' | \'daily_puzzle\' | \'clean_game\' | \'sportsmanship\' | \'puzzle_streak\' | \'admin_bonus\';\n46: }\n47: \n48: export interface GameState {\n49:   fen: string;\n50:   history: string[];\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines."
    thinking: "**Defining Theme Modules**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on defining modular themes. I\'ve got \"Attack on Titan,\" \"Batman Gotham City,\" and a \"Classic\" theme figured out, and the concept of cross-compatibility is coming into focus. I need to make sure independent piece selection for \"White\" and \"Black\" will work smoothly within this system, especially for crossovers.\n\n\n**Refining Piece & Board**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of piece and board design, looking at the existing types and components to ensure compatibility. In `/src/types/chess.ts`, I\'ll update the `BoardThemeId` and `PieceThemeId` to accommodate crossover selection using `whitePieceTheme` and `blackPieceTheme`. I need to ensure that the Gotham City board design looks really sharp with dark squares using `#111827`, light squares: `#374151`, and a Bat-Signal highlight using `rgba(234, 179, 8, 0.5)`. I\'m working on full SVG rendering for Batman theme pieces.\n\n\n"
