    thinking: "**Analyzing Movement Glitch**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `activePieces` data structure and how it\'s updated during user moves. I\'m carefully reviewing the `onMove` function, which is the core of this process. The two main ways a move happens are through clicking or dragging. I\'m comparing the logic paths when `onMove` is triggered by a click or drag operation.\n\n\n**Investigating State Updates**\n\nI\'ve shifted my attention to how the `useEffect` hook in `ChessBoard.tsx` interacts with the `lastMove` state, and how the `activePieces` state updates in response to `game.fen()`. I\'m concerned about cases where `lastMove` might be stale or when changes in `game.fen()` are triggered by something other than a user move, such as undo, redo, reset, or an opponent\'s move. This also has effects on the piece animation.\n\n\n"
