  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Joker\'s Presence**\n\nI\'m focusing on the peculiarity of the Joker piece, specifically how the King figure in the Batman set, meant to represent him, appears off. I\'m investigating the potential causes, considering the visual representation doesn\'t quite capture his essence as the Clown Prince of Crime. I\'m seeking the critical components of the depiction which create this disparity.\n\n\n**Refining the Joker\'s Essence**\n\nI\'ve homed in on specific design choices in the Joker piece. The floating eyes and the disconnected grin, devoid of any defined face or chin, are now the primary focus. This unconventional rendering, with a mane of spiky green hair where a face should be, strikes me as a significant departure from the source material and it\'s something I\'m finding quite provocative. I\'m considering why these choices were made and what effect they have.\n\n\n**Reimagining the Pieces**\n\nNow, I\'m shifting to how the Joker and his rogue\'s gallery should actually be represented. I\'m thinking beyond the initial unsettling design and the overall style of the existing chess pieces. I\'m focusing on creating instantly recognizable figures with clear royal chess silhouettes, something that blends the classic chess form with the Batman/Joker character aesthetics. I\'m sketching out a dignified King with sharp details, aiming for a design that captures the essence of the Joker.\n\n\n**Defining Character Visuals**\n\nI\'m now concretely defining the character visuals. The Joker\'s pale face, emerald hair, and crimson grin are central, augmented by a twisted crown and a crisp SVG design. Harley Quinn\'s jester cowl and diamond motifs are taking shape, as are The Riddler\'s bowler hat and question-mark staff, then Bane\'s venom armor and a menacing Knight horse-head, while the Rook embodies the Arkham Asylum. High-contrast elements and clean gradients should make the pieces pop.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 29
      nanos: 274661893
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
